[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[33AI have compiled the audit findings into\r\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc9ae5bc917ca27d6;file:///Users/brett/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/1d6e0269-57af-497f-9e2e-3bccc3aa26e5/goldfish_review_report.md\u0007~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/1d6e0269-57af-497f-9e2e-3bccc3aa26e5/goldfish_review_report.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007. Please review the\r\n  findings there and choose how you would like to proceed:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mComment directly on the file\u001b[m: Review\r\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc9ae5ac917ca2623;file:///Users/brett/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/1d6e0269-57af-497f-9e2e-3bccc3aa26e5/goldfish_review_report.md\u0007~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/1d6e0269-57af-497f-9e2e-3bccc3aa26e5/goldfish_review_report.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 in chat or the file\r\n  and leave comments/edits to approve, reject, or contest specific items.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mAuto accept\u001b[m: Reply \"auto accept\" to batch-apply all proposed fixes (skipping contested items).\n\u001b[94D\u001b[1mContinue to next phase\u001b[m: Reply \"continue\" or \"no changes\" to proceed without applying fixes.\u001b[K\n\u001b[91D\u001b[1mInter"]
[0.0, "o", "active breakdown\u001b[m: Reply \"interactive breakdown\" for a guided, item-by-item walkthrough in chat with detailed\r\n  explanations for each proposed edit or contested finding before making decisions.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mCustom instruction / Wildcard request\u001b[m: Reply with any custom instruction, question, or out-of-band request.\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> interactive\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 15s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1m### Breakdown Item 1 (of 12): Replace Ineffective \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_DIV\u001b[39m Pacing with NVIC IRQ Gating and Calibrate \u001b[8b\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94;1mrp23xx_adc.c\u001b[39m Claims [\u001b[94megm-zoom-out\u001b[39m / \u001b[94megm-inventive-catalyst\u001b[39m / \u001b[94megm-design\u001b[39m / \u001b[94megm-codebase-details\u001b[39m]\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mScope:\u001b[m \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2bba671402d21f61;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L25-L66"]
[0.0, "o", "2\u0007Lines 25–662\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 (\u001b[94m## The Problem\u001b[m, \u001b[94m## Goals\u001b[m, \u001b[94m### 3. Boot Sequence\u001b[m, \u001b[94m### 4.1 ADC Subsystem Mitigations\u001b[m, \u001b[94m## Non-\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mFunctional Requirements\u001b[m, \u001b[94m### Additional Resources\u001b[m, Target Files #13, #17, #30)\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mDescription:\u001b[m The design currently states that \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk9ed85f546316f6bb;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L169-L320\u0007nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c:169-320\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 runs the ADC in\r\n  continuous free-running mode (\u001b[94mADC_CS_START_MANY\u001b[m) and that writing \u001b[94mputreg32(0x00ffff00, RP23XX_ADC_DIV)\u001b[m in\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mrp23xx_bringup.c\u001b[m paces conversions to \u001b[94m~732.42 Hz\u001b[m. In the actual upstream driver, \u001b[94mrp23xx_adc.c\u001b[m never sets\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_CS_START_MANY\u001b[m: \u001b[94minterrupt_handler()\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkaa3f9bb9795d259d;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L234\u0007line 234\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007) unconditionally calls "]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[94mget_next_channel()\u001b[m, which writes\r\n  single-shot \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_CS_START_ONCE\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk68fbf49c9af7b3e8;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L304\u0007line 304\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007) even when \u001b[94mau_receive()\u001b[m returns \u001b[94m-ENOMEM\u001b[m on a full software FIFO. On\r\n  RP2350 hardware, \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_DIV\u001b[m only paces free-running \u001b[94mSTART_MANY\u001b[m conversions and does not delay \u001b[94mSTART_ONCE\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  triggers (\u001b[94m2 µs\u001b[m/sample). Additionally, the ISR in \u001b[94mrp23xx_adc.c\u001b[m is named \u001b[94minterrupt_handler()\u001b[m (not \u001b[94madc_interrupt()\u001b[m),\r\n  and \u001b[94mremove_\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[11D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[12A\u001b[9C\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk7a6ad457320d43c8;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L25-L662\u0007Lines 25–662\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\n\u001b[27C\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf91ba9ffb13755e0;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L169-L320\u0007nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c:169-320\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\n\n\u001b[47D\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jka75a2b5aed09e92c;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L234\u0007line 234\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[3Z\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jke0d4a986006826d;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L304\u0007line 304\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\n\n\u001b[35D\u001b[94mdevice(dev)\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[22D\u001b[?2026l"]
