[0.1, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[33A\u001b[38C\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk3172c867f3e6498;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L304\u0007line 304\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\n\n\u001b[30C\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk73a2735dc3de6cfa;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L538\u0007lines 538, 563\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[42D\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd762809b969203b9;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L176\u0007line 176\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t reading 5 samples (\u001b[94mmsgs[0]\u001b[m discar\r\n\n⢿ \n\n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[33A  single-shot \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_CS_START_ONCE\u001b[m (\u001b]8;id=jk3f1b27b17222348d;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L304\u001b\\\u001b[4;34;4ml\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mi\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mn\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4me\u001b[m\u001b[34;4m \u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m3\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m0\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m4\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\) even when \u001b[94mau_receive()\u001b[m returns \u001b[94m-ENOMEM\u001b[m on a full software FIFO. On\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  RP2350 hardware, \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_DIV\u001b[m only paces free-running \u001b[94mSTART_MANY\u001b[m conversions and does not delay \u001b[94mSTART_ONCE\u001b[m\r\n  triggers (\u001b[94m2 µs\u001b[m/sample). Additionally, the ISR in \u001b[94mrp23xx_adc.c\u001b[m is named \u001b[94minterrupt_handler()\u001b[m (not \u001b[94madc_interrupt()\u001b[m),\r\n  and \u001b[94mremove_device(dev)\u001b[m is called from \u001b[94mmy_shutdown()\u001b[m / \u001b[94mmy_rxint(dev, false)\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkdbe7048e084d200f;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L538\u0007lines 538, 563\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007) while\r\n  \u001b[94minterrupt_handler()\u001b[m checks \u001b[94mg_active_count == 0\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8a"]
[0.0, "o", "6af0c22ab7cc0;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_adc.c#L176\u0007line 176\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007).\r\n  • \u001b[1mAI Suggestion:\u001b[m \u001b[94mPROPOSE FIX\u001b[m\r\n  • \u001b[1mExplanation & Justification:\u001b[m Because \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_DIV\u001b[m does not slow down \u001b[94mSTART_ONCE\u001b[m writes, keeping \u001b[94m/dev/adc0\u001b[m open\r\n  with \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO\u001b[m unmasked in the NVIC still fires \u001b[94m500,000 IRQ/s\u001b[m continuously. Since the firmware builds in\r\n  flat mode (\u001b[94mCONFIG_BUILD_FLAT=y\u001b[m), \u001b[94mbargraphd\u001b[m can keep \u001b[94m/dev/adc0\u001b[m open (avoiding the \u001b[94mmy_shutdown()\u001b[m / \u001b[94mremove_device()\u001b[m\r\n  race) and gate \u001b[94mRP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO\u001b[m at the NVIC via \u001b[94mup_disable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m and\r\n  \u001b[94mup_enable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m (\u001b[94m<nuttx/irq.h>\u001b[m and \u001b[94m<arch/rp23xx/irq.h>\u001b[m):\n\u001b[71D1. Immediately after \u001b[94mopen(\"/dev/adc0\", O_RDONLY)\u001b[m, call \u001b[94mup_disable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m. The single in-\r\n\u001b[6Cflight conversion completes in \u001b[94m2 µs\u001b[m and pends in "]
[0.0, "o", "the NVIC without firing an ISR during the \u001b[94m20 ms\u001b[m sleep window.\r\n\u001b[6C2. On each \u001b[94m50 Hz\u001b[m burst in \u001b[94mbargraph_sample_adc()\u001b[m: call \u001b[94mioctl(adc_fd, ANIOC_RESET_FIFO, 0)\u001b[m, call\n\u001b[94D\u001b[94mup_enable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m, read \u001b[94m5\u001b[m \u001b[94mstruct adc_msg_s\u001b[m entries (\u001b[94m~10 µs\u001b[m), immediately call\n\u001b[94D\u001b[94mup_disable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m, discard \u001b[94mmsgs[0]\u001b[m (the 1 sample latched at the end of the previous cycle),\r\n\u001b[6Cand average the 4 fresh samples \u001b[94mmsgs[1..4]\u001b[m.\n\u001b[43D3. On \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m, call \u001b[94mup_enable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m right before \u001b[94mclose(adc_fd)\u001b[m so \u001b[94minterrupt_handler()\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cexecutes its \u001b[94mg_active_count == 0\u001b[m teardown cleanly.\n\u001b[50DThis reduces the ADC interrupt rate from \u001b[94m500,000 IRQ/s\u001b[m to \u001b[94m250 IRQ/s\u001b[m (\u001b[94m99.95%\u001b[m reduction) and reduces per-tick\r\n\u001b[6Csample acquisition blocking from \u001b[94m5.5 ms\u001b[m to \u001b[94m~10 µs\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mProposed Edit:\u001b[m\n\u001b[12D• Remove \u001b[94mputreg32(0x00ffff00, RP23XX_ADC_DIV)\u001b"]
[0.0, "o", "[m from \u001b[94mrp23xx_bringup.c\u001b[m (Target Files #13 and #17) and from the\r\n\u001b[6Cboot sequence diagram / prose (lines 33, 220, 242–245, 378, 509, 538–542).\n\u001b[74D• Update Problem #7 (line 25), Goals (line 33), Section 4.1.3–4.1.4 (lines 242–250), Non-Functional\n\u001b[99DRequirements (lines 378–379), Additional Resources (line 391), and Target File #29/#30 (\u001b[94mbargraph_internal.h\u001b[m /\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mbargraph_main.c\u001b[m, lines 635, 660–662) to describe \u001b[94mrp23xx_adc.c\u001b[m's \u001b[94mSTART_ONCE\u001b[m re-trigger loop in\n\u001b[93D\u001b[94minterrupt_handler()\u001b[m -> \u001b[94mget_next_channel()\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmy_shutdown()\u001b[m -> \u001b[94mremove_device(dev)\u001b[m, and NVIC IRQ gating\n\u001b[99D(\u001b[94mup_disable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m / \u001b[94mup_enable_irq(RP23XX_ADC_IRQ_FIFO)\u001b[m) reading 5 samples (\u001b[94mmsgs[0]\u001b[m discarded,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mmsgs[1\u001b[m\r\n\n⢿  \u001b[90mWorking...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Press ? to see keyboard shortcuts.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────"]
